{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "היום הזה", :translit "ha-yom ha-zeh", :gloss "this day"} {:he "אחל", :translit "achel", :gloss "I will begin"} {:he "בחמה", :translit "be-chamah", :gloss "with the sun"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אחל", :b "בחמה"} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: 'יום' (day) is read as 'חמה' (sun), since daylight equals the sun"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'היום הזה' (Deuteronomy 2:25) is read as an allusion to God stopping the sun for Moses. Genesis 1:5 defines light as 'יום' (day), and the sun is the celestial body governing the day (Genesis 1:16), so 'day' can signify 'sun.' The gematria equating 'אחל' with 'בחמה' confirms this reading: the beginning of Moses' military campaign was marked by the sun standing still.", :sources ["Genesis 1:5" "Genesis 1:16" "Deuteronomy 2:25"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אחל", :translit "achel", :gloss "I will begin / I will profane"} {:he "אחל גדלך", :translit "achel gedalkha", :gloss "I will proclaim My greatness"} {:he "ולא אחל את שם קדשי", :translit "ve-lo achel et shem kedoshi", :gloss "and I will not profane My holy name"} {:he "ואת שם קדשי אודיע", :translit "ve-et shem kedoshi odia", :gloss "and My holy name I will make known"} {:he "ולא אחל את שם קדשי עוד", :translit "ve-lo achel et shem kedoshi od", :gloss "and I will not profane My holy name anymore"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["אחל" "אחל גדלך" "ולא אחל את שם קדשי"]}], :frame {:text "Joshua 10:12–13 records the sun standing still for Joshua. The three-fold occurrence of 'אחל' links Deuteronomy 2:25, Exodus 33:19 ('אחל גדלך'), and Ezekiel 39:7 ('ולא אחל את שם קדשי עוד'). Ezekiel 39:7 pairs 'ולא אחל את שם קדשי' with 'ואת שם קדשי אודיע' — the sanctification of God's name. Psalm 19:2 declares 'השמים מספרים כבוד אל' (the heavens declare the glory of God), establishing that celestial wonders make God's name known. The sun standing for Moses thus parallels Joshua 10:12–13: in both cases the miracle publicized God